    "created_at": "2026-09-28T21:40:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-28T21:40:04Z",
    "body": "I found my way here because I'm revamping Chromium's implementation to look more like the spec around activation behavior. And I rediscovered the problem from the OP where activation behavior for buttons currently always exists. I'm supportive of the `has activation behavior` algorithm idea, but as mentioned above, that would also need to be checked in the middle of [event dispatch](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#dispatching-events), not just before it runs, so that dynamic changes are respected. As part of my refactoring, I'll try to put together a more comprehensive set of WPTs for button activation, and I'll mark it `.tentative` for now while this issue is open.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
